    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry Fitzgerald Stack are delighted to bring to market this 4 bedroom, 3 bathroom detached residence located in an idyllic countryside setting with scenic views.\nThe spacious and well-proportioned property is located 3km from the village of Mountcollins, and 9km from the market town of Abbeyfeale, the main N21 route, and the Limerick Greenway. Heritage towns and other landmarks are within a short drive away - Newcastle West and Crag Cave are each 20 mins, Tralee and Listowel are each 30 mins, and Killarney is 45 mins. Ground Floor comprises: Conservatory, Living Room, Sitting Room, Kitchen/Dining Room, Utility and bathroom with whb, w/c & shower. 1st floor comprises: 4 bedrooms (2 spacious doubles and 2 compact doubles) and main bathroom with whb, w/c & bathtub. The attic is floored and accessible by full-size staircase with built-in wardrobes underneath. The large open plan space is suitable for a variety of uses and has a separate w/c & whb.\nThe residence has the benefit of both oil fired central heating & 2 solid fuel stoves (one of which has a back boiler), private water supply, on-site biocycle system and double glazed upvc windows.\nThe 24sqm garage is beautifully finished in stone - ideal for storage / DIY purposes while another 20sqm metal clad store also provides for additional storage.\nThe property enjoys mature lawns, trees & shrubs. The south facing porch and concreted area creates the perfect sun trap.\nViewing of this fine property is highly recommended and is strictly by appointment only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nConservatory - 2.78m x 2.29m\nwith stone walls, original floor tiles, teak door & windows\n\nLiving Room - 5.02m x 4.47m\nwith solid fuel stove, redbrick arch surround between living room & kitchen, wooden flooring, fitted units, alcove shelving & window\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - 4.23m x 3.79m\nwith beech fitted kitchen, Kensington dual gas & electric cooker, ceramic wall & floor tiles, half glazed door to rear & window\n\nUtility Room - 3.63m x 2.90m\nwasher & dryer, ceramic floor tiles, & window\n\nBathroom - 2.80m x 1.06m\nwith Triton T90 XR shower, ceramic wall & floor tiles, whb, w/c & window\n\nLounge / Sitting Room - 4.91m x 2.76m\nRedbrick feature surround fireplace, double door solid fuel stove (with back boiler), wooden flooring & 2 windows\n\nLanding - 4.92m x 1.53m\nwith carpet flooring & window\n\nBedroom 1 - 6.41m x 3.59m\ndouble room with wardrobes, wooden flooring, 3 windows, and staircase to attic\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.05m x 3.62m\ndouble room with wooden flooring & 2 windows\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.78m x 2.54m\ncompact double room with wooden flooring, fitted units & window\n\nFamily Bathroom - 2.74m x 1.77m\nwith ceramic wall & floor tiles, pumped shower, bath, whb, w/c & window\n\nAttic - \nLarge open plan area - floored with 4 velux windows. Separate w/c with whb & window\n\nGarage - 6m x 4m\nBlock built garage beautifully finished with stone, A roof, pedestrian door, roller door & 2 windows\n\nStore - 5m x 4m\nsheeted storehouse\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Peaceful rural area with exceptional views of the surrounding countryside</li><li>Views of Carrauntoohil, Slieve Mish, and Mount Brandon from its elevated position</li><li>South facing residence</li><li>Excellent high-speed fibre connection</li><li>Smart meter</li><li>No light pollution</li><li>Large open plan attic area - floored with 4 velux windows.</li><li>24sqm stone built garage & 20sqm sheeted storehouse</li><li>Mature lawns, trees and shrubs</li><li>3km from the village of Mountcollins</li><li>9km from the market town of Abbeyfeale and main N21 route</li><li>Tralee and Killarney are within a short drive way - 30 mins & 45 mins respectively</ul>"
      },
